{"title":"Career Roadmap · Customs Executive","role":"Customs Executive","summary":"A Customs Executive supports businesses with customs-related documentation, import/export procedures, shipment clearance, classification, duty calculations, compliance and coordination with customs brokers, freight forwarders, ports, airports and government authorities.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Com (Bachelor of Commerce)","Course":"B.Com – Foreign Trade / International Business"},"about":[{"label":"Alignment","text":"Very Strong"},{"label":"Typical Entry Level","text":"Customs Executive / Customs Documentation Executive / Import-Export Executive"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Customs Executive supports businesses with customs-related documentation, import/export procedures, shipment clearance, classification, duty calculations, compliance and coordination with customs brokers, freight forwarders, ports, airports and government authorities."},{"type":"p","text":"B.Com Foreign Trade / International Business is highly relevant because it provides exposure to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"International trade"},{"text":"Import/export procedures"},{"text":"Trade documentation"},{"text":"International finance"},{"text":"Logistics"},{"text":"Business law"},{"text":"Foreign exchange"},{"text":"Customs procedures"}]},{"type":"note","label":"A key distinction is important","text":"a private-sector Customs Executive is generally an import-export/customs operations role. It is different from a government Customs Officer, which is a government service position recruited through specified competitive examinations and recruitment processes."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Role","Main Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Trade/Logistics Intern"},{"text":"Trade fundamentals"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Import-Export Intern"},{"t